    "text": "A bat moving at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> towards a wall sends a sound signal of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>Hz</mtext></math> towards it. On reflection, it hears a sound of frequency <math><mi>f</mi></math>. The value of <math><mi>f</mi></math> in <math> <mrow> <mtext>Hz</mtext> </mrow> </math> is close to<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mtext>speed&#160;of&#160;sound</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>320</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">)</mo></math>"
